            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>docker-compose.yml</h2>
                    <p>Example compose file defining multiple services (order, inventory, db, rabbitmq) and shared volumes.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">version: '3.8'

services:
  orderservice:
    build: ./src/OrderService
    ports:
      - "5001:80"
    environment:
      - ConnectionStrings__Database=Server=db;Database=Orders;User=sa;Password=Password123!
      - RabbitMQ__Host=rabbitmq
    depends_on:
      - db
      - rabbitmq

  inventoryservice:
    build: ./src/InventoryService
    ports:
      - "5002:80"
    environment:
      - ConnectionStrings__Database=Server=db;Database=Inventory;User=sa;Password=Password123!
    depends_on:
      - db

  db:
    image: mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest
    environment:
      - ACCEPT_EULA=Y
      - SA_PASSWORD=Password123!
    volumes:
      - sqldata:/var/opt/mssql

  rabbitmq:
    image: rabbitmq:3-management
    ports:
      - "15672:15672"

volumes:
  sqldata:</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Commands</h2>
                    <p>Common docker-compose commands to bring up, rebuild, view logs, and tear down the development environment.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Start all services
docker-compose up -d

# Rebuild and start
docker-compose up -d --build

# View logs
docker-compose logs -f orderservice

# Stop all
docker-compose down

# Stop and remove volumes
docker-compose down -v</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Health Checks</h2>
                    <p>Compose supports healthchecks; this example shows how to declare checks and use depends_on with condition for startup ordering during development (not a production-ready init strategy).</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">services:
  orderservice:
    build: ./src/OrderService
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "curl", "-f", "http://localhost/health"]
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 10s
      retries: 3
      start_period: 40s
    depends_on:
      db:
        condition: service_healthy</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Compose orchestrates multi-container apps.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use depends_on for startup order.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Health checks ensure dependencies are ready.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
